<div id="dashboards" class="docs-section">
  <h2>Dashboards</h2>
  <p>Dashboards show charts built from saved SQL queries. Each card on a dashboard is one query drawn as a pie, bar, line or scatter chart, or as a table.</p>

  <h3>Accessing Dashboards</h3>
  <p>Click <strong>Dashboards</strong> in the profile dropdown. Pick a dashboard from the list to open it.</p>

  <h3>Building Dashboards</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Viewing dashboards and writing the SQL behind them are separate grants.</li>
    <li>An author writes a query, runs it to preview the rows and the chart, and saves it.</li>
    <li>The first column is the label or x value, the second the value, and an optional third the series.</li>
    <li>Queries run under a read-only login, with a timeout and a row limit.</li>
  </ul>
</div>
